Original commit body from 698c297c8174f1a95802775985af675d0fa8f0e2:

41 of 481 invocations in .git/AUTOPR_HISTORY.jsonl carry final_state=merged
with exit_code=1, and every one of those merged_shas is an ancestor of
origin/dev (control: 358 of 359 for merged+exit 0). The merge landed; auto-pr
reported failure. Most recent was yesterday.

set -euo pipefail plus two bare commands in the tail that runs after
_autopr_state_final="merged". `git checkout "$base"` refuses whenever a dirty
file differs between the feature branch and the base, which a modified tracker
.ops file is, and which this working tree ordinarily has. `read -p "Retry?"`
returns 1 at EOF, so on every non-interactive run the retry prompt was an abort
rather than a question -- at attempt 1 of a documented 3, meaning that loop has
never run in production.

Once the merge has landed the outcome is decided, so the housekeeping now runs
through _autopr_post_merge, whose `if !` context makes bash ignore set -e for
the whole callee body including anything it calls, and the merged paths exit 0
explicitly instead of inheriting branch cleanup's status. A boundary rather
than three guards, because the defect is the absence of one -- and the
structural test pinning it found a fourth call site,
_autopr_handle_already_merged, that reading the post-merge tails had missed.

gov_cleanup additionally recorded its terminal state after its housekeeping, so
an abort there discarded the merged fact and landed on `unknown` instead. It
records first now.

The harness that owns cleanup_local ran set -uo pipefail for its whole life.
Without the -e it cannot observe an abort-shaped defect at all, which is why
the one test file covering this function watched the class go by for six weeks.
It runs production flags now, and the new behavioral tests drive the real
extracted functions under them.

Both surfaces INV-rahib named on 2026-08-02 were already fixed (560c18cbb2,
c539caf0b7); this is a different mechanism found by reading the convergence
ledger that commit added and nothing had ever consumed. The item stays violated
for its second class -- 14 runs ending in no declared terminal state -- filed as
WI-nazoj, with the missing ledger reader as WI-lapap.

